    \field{abstract}{%
    A report on the analysis of statistical data on vulnerabilities from public
  data sources has been presented to develop a mathematical model for
  penetration testing. Current trends in attacks and threats have been
  analyzed. Attack automation issues and trends in the search for an improved
  algorithm for automated penetration testing have been explored. A technique
  for assessing information security risk, considering additional criteria
  implemented using machine learning elements, has been proposed. A criticality
  criterion has been highlighted, which improves the exploit attack module in
  the penetration testing. Sorting identified vulnerabilities according to the
  proposed criteria allows improvement of the characteristics of automated
  penetration tests based on exploit kit attacks.%
